      "writtenOn": "2026-10-02T18:29:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To add to what Greg said, the design doc for SkSurface creation from an SkRecorder states that the surface type will be specific to the recorder\u0027s backend. If a client wants to explicitly create a CPU-backed image, they need a CPU-based recorder. There is backend-selection enum passed in to the context\u0027s makeRecorder() function so that they can create CPU recorders when on a GPU context. This is separate from whether or not it\u0027s a SkRecorder member function or a static function, but I prefer the member function in this case.\n\nI think this model for backend selection is sufficient to start, but we could also consider exposing the backend selection as a parameter to the surface/image factories too.",
      "parentUuid": "0b491846_1e06921c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 61
